      "attribution": "Written for EducateOS.",
      "body": "Read each mRNA codon (three bases) from left to right, starting at the start codon AUG. These are the codons you need for this unit; the full table has 64.\n\nStart: AUG = Met (methionine), which also begins every protein\nAla (alanine): GCU, GCC, GCA, GCG\nGlu (glutamic acid): GAA, GAG\nGly (glycine): GGU, GGC, GGA, GGG\nHis (histidine): CAU, CAC\nIle (isoleucine): AUU, AUC, AUA\nLeu (leucine): CUU, CUC, CUA, CUG, UUA, UUG\nLys (lysine): AAA, AAG\nPhe (phenylalanine): UUU, UUC\nPro (proline): CCU, CCC, CCA, CCG\nSer (serine): UCU, UCC, UCA, UCG, AGU, AGC\nThr (threonine): ACU, ACC, ACA, ACG\nTrp (tryptophan): UGG\nVal (valine): GUU, GUC, GUA, GUG\nStop (end of the protein): UAA, UAG, UGA\n\nBase-pairing rules. DNA to DNA: A pairs with T, G pairs with C. DNA template to mRNA: A to U, T to A, G to C, C to G.",
